/-- Before-mesh normalized zero-base Baillon-Haddad endpoint from support,
smooth upper model, selected-gradient semantics, and Lipschitz selected
gradients on an open convex chart.

This is the lower-level Lan Lemma 5.8 endpoint after the supporting plane has
already been subtracted, so `Φ z = 0`, `B z = 0`, and `Φ` is nonnegative on
the chart. Search audit: checked the pre-searched downstream candidates
`open_zero_base_endpoint_energy_le_twice_L_gap`,
`open_zero_base_self_bound_non_circular`, and
`open_normalized_zero_base_endpoint_energy_from_support_upper_lipschitz`, plus
